 "prompt": "You are answering a biomedical research question.\n\nQuestion: Could different follow-up modalities play a role in the diagnosis of asymptomatic endometrial cancer relapses?\n\nAnswer \"yes\", \"no\", or \"maybe\", and give your confidence from 0 to 100 that your answer is correct.\n\nRespond with only a JSON object and no other text, in exactly this format:\n{\"answer\": \"yes\" or \"no\" or \"maybe\", \"confidence\": integer from 0 to 100}",
 "session_persisted": false,
 "text": "\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls\n\n<｜DSML｜function_callsBased on my biomedical knowledge, endometrial cancer follow-up typically involves regular physical exams, imaging (CT, MRI, PET), and sometimes tumor marker tests (CA-125). Different follow-up modalities can indeed play a role in diagnosing asymptomatic relapses, as some modalities (like imaging) can detect recurrences before symptoms appear, while others (like physical exams) may only detect symptomatic relapses. However, the evidence on optimal follow-up strategies is mixed, with some studies showing limited benefit of intensive surveillance.\n\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"confidence\": 75}",
